DevOps Interview Preparation – Tool 3

Git (Basics + Advanced) | 0–2 Years Experience

In DevOps, Git is not optional.
Every CI/CD pipeline, Infrastructure as Code, and cloud automation starts with Git.

Interviewers don’t check only commands — they check how you think about version control.

Focus: Git Interview Questions (Mixed – Basics + Advanced)

• What is Git and why is it important in DevOps?
• Difference between Git and GitHub
• What is a repository?
• Difference between local, remote, and central repo
• What is git init and git clone?
• Explain git status, git add, and git commit
• What is .gitignore and why is it used?
• What is branching in Git?
• Difference between main and feature branch
• How do you create and delete branches?
• What is a merge? Types of merge
• What is a merge conflict and how do you resolve it?
• Difference between git merge and git rebase
• What is git stash? When do you use it?
• What is git cherry-pick?
• Difference between git fetch and git pull
• What is a detached HEAD state?
• What is git reset vs git revert?
• How do you undo a wrong commit?
• What is tagging in Git?
• Explain Git workflow used in your project
• How do you manage Git in a team environment?
• Common Git mistakes beginners make
• Real-world Git issue you faced and how you fixed it

💡 Interview Tip:
If you can clearly explain:
 branching strategy + conflict resolution + rollback
you already look production-ready, even as a fresher.
